 S~S README metadata: The SimpleSal software is educational software.

=====================

  S~S About this README file

  There are two major parts to this README, each section relates to one part or the other:

    1) the traditional background information about the repo blob using traditional terminology;

    2) the nontraditional philosophy that leads to a path: developers may request their personal
       SimpleSal App be added to the public SimpleSal ecosystem as a GitHub repository.

=====================

  S~S The Elevator Pitch

------------------------------------------

 SimpleSal is software that supports simple experimental development of signal/sensor algorithms.

 SimpleSal software co-exists with an Arduino application's software.  it provides a sense of Time,
 and, it enables Event-based software algorithms that implement the interactions devices require.

 This basis in software removes the hardware from consideration by the developer: there is no
 interrupt circuitry between the device and the processor, no interrupt controller to satisfy.

 There is a virtual interrupt controller (VIC), within the SimpleSal software, constructed from
 self-contained software.  The VIC ACTS LiKE an interrupt controller (e.g., dispatch handlers
 based on masks and enables); when it is, at a Time chosen by the developer, granted Agency.

------------------------------------------

  S~S The 5-minute Trade Show Presentation

------------------------------------------

 SimpleSal is also a laboratory for developing skills commonly expected of a software developer.

 The moderate complexity of the entire SimpleSal ecosystem enables a developer to take a step
 towards operating system software development task requirements, outside the software itself.

 For example, the transition to a "SimpleSal App" from a standard Arduino App requires:

    you read the complete, specific, step-by-step, and proven directions, if you can find them.

 Just kidding, the transition requires a few steps described by documents within the source tree.

    1) this repo's managed object be placed in the App directory as the directory SimpleSal;
    2) 3 text files be copied and then renamed, from SimpleSal up into the App directory;
    3) copy-and-paste changes be made around, not to, the setup and loop functions in the App;

 This will create a buildable SimpleSal App that co-exists with ssTEA and keeps track of Time.

------------------------------------------

  S~S The last-chance pitch at the table in the back of Trade Show ballroom

------------------------------------------

 Now you've heard of all the concepts that SimpleSal is intended to introduce to a user.

 Now you've heard of all the knowledge that the user must have to use SimpleSal.

 The rest of this README introduces the basic concepts common to a repository of software.

 Any repo's structure and content is a software engineering decision and a software decision.

